{
  "sticker": "bear",
  "called": "the bear cub",
  "skeleton": "sitting cub facing the viewer: root at the seat; body with belly squash; head on the body (neck), face with eyes and mouth; armL/armR at the shoulders; legL/legR (stretched forward, paw pads showing) at the hips on the root.",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a bear cub character. Draw this exact bear cub as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the body: the round sitting body with its cream tummy, facing the viewer as in image 1, without head, arms or legs; its top, normally under the head, rounded.\n2. the head: the round head with its two round ears, cream muzzle and black nose, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no mouth — keep the muzzle, the nose and the rosy cheeks; its bottom edge rounded.\n3. one arm: the cub's arm on the right of image 1, resting down beside the tummy, with its paw, with a rounded shoulder.\n4. one leg: the sitting leg on the right of image 1, stretched forward with its big paw pad showing, with a rounded hip.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a bear cub character; image 2 shows the same bear cub cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the bear cub's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the bear cub in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the cub's left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a content, slightly sleepy half-lidded dark eye.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small happy smile under the nose.\n7. the mouth wide open in a big yawn: a tall oval, the inside pink.\n8. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n9. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n10. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
  ],
